 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 7680,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The first copied byte in the scene record is $05. The caller starts executing one byte later."
  },
  {
   "address": 7681,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Save and reload the caller stack pointer, set the room palette, install the raster handler and enable sprites 5\u20137 in the bank at $4000. Apply the colour lookup and initialize the tentacle state."
  },
  {
   "address": 7684,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Restore the stack and use the three room palette colours at $D021\u2013$D023. Fill the glyph and score pointers, install the room raster behaviour and enable sprites 5\u20137."
  },
  {
   "address": 9658,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Copy three bytes per row through the source and destination pointers and decrement each pointer by three. The row counter controls the extra step between 21-row sprite records."
  },
  {
   "address": 9907,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Copy three bytes per row and advance both pointers. After 21 rows advance again to skip the sprite record padding."
  },
  {
   "address": 10163,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Request sound $8A, multiply the selection by 20 and use a table from $29D8 to set sprite coordinates. The $2A5E mode changes which subset is written."
  },
  {
   "address": 10480,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Wait through the scene timing routine with count $32, call the shared routine at $0ECD and jump back to scene initialization."
  },
  {
   "address": 10491,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Count down A in $2DAF. Complement $2A5B on each iteration and wait and poll the joystick on the zero phase."
  },
  {
   "address": 10516,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Count down A in $2DAF and call $256D after each timer wait and joystick sample on alternate phases of $2A5B."
  },
  {
   "address": 10544,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Wait and sample the joystick A times, invoking $2942 after each timer delay."
  },
  {
   "address": 10562,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Every third call, AND bytes at $6C81\u2013$6D3F with a changing mask made by XORing CIA1 timer A low and the raster counter."
  },
  {
   "address": 10597,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Read CIA1 port A with all keyboard column outputs high, invert the active-low bits and compare with the previous sample at $2A60 before updating that byte."
  },
  {
   "address": 10849,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Multiply the pose index A by 90, add $3200 and copy the resulting record to $44\u2013$9D after synchronizing to raster."
  },
  {
   "address": 12373,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "This scene record ends with the eleven byte marker copied by the unpacker at $0DDE."
  },
  {
   "address": 16384,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The first page of the screen matrix for the background in VIC bank $4000. Its character codes index the scene colour lookup when the display is initialized."
  },
  {
   "address": 16640,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Screen matrix offsets $100\u2013$1FF. The VIC reads these as character codes and the palette routine processes a page at a time."
  },
  {
   "address": 16896,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Screen matrix offsets $200\u2013$2FF. The screen maps into the glyph data at $7800."
  },
  {
   "address": 17152,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The last page of the screen matrix, including the hardware sprite pointers at $43F8\u2013$43FF."
  },
  {
   "address": 17408,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "First sixteen sprite records after the room screen. The rendered pieces include curved and extended movement shapes."
  },
  {
   "address": 18432,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen shapes including bent limbs and head silhouettes, laid out in 64-byte records."
  },
  {
   "address": 19456,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "A run of sprite fragments of legs and arms for the tentacle-room player animation."
  },
  {
   "address": 20480,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen shapes continuing the pose table, including several paired lower body figures."
  },
  {
   "address": 21504,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Middle bank of rendered movement fragments, with a long curved arm at pointer $59."
  },
  {
   "address": 22528,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen pieces of sprite movement and body posing in adjacent 64-byte slots."
  },
  {
   "address": 23552,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Tentacle-room sprite part masks for pointers $70\u2013$7F. The leg shapes change orientation between successive records."
  },
  {
   "address": 24576,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen records including the alternately curled and outstretched body pieces at the end of this range."
  },
  {
   "address": 25600,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Middle-to-high range of body-part masks, with some blank records between the visible pieces."
  },
  {
   "address": 26624,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sprite parts around pointer $A9, which the scene writes to $43F8 at $2AE6."
  },
  {
   "address": 27776,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The scene filters bytes $6C81\u2013$6D3F at $295F, using the timer and raster as a mask during the sprite-erasure effect."
  },
  {
   "address": 27968,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The unpacked picture stream initializes $6D40\u2013$6EFF to zero. These bytes are still zero in the play capture."
  },
  {
   "address": 28416,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen extended and folded shapes near the end of the room sprite bank, spaced by $40 bytes."
  },
  {
   "address": 29440,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "High sprite slots including claw-like, curved and extended tentacle shapes."
  },
  {
   "address": 30464,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Colour table whose entries are indexed by the bytes in the room screen matrix. The scene selects its page at $1E6D."
  },
  {
   "address": 30720,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The scene character glyph store for VIC bank $4000 and character-base bits 3\u20131 of $D018 set to 7. A character occupies eight consecutive bytes."
  },
  {
   "address": 31744,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The top half of this scene set, from character code $80. The eight-byte glyph slots are used for the scene-specific objects and screen details."
  },
  {
   "address": 47029,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Repeated $06 bytes at $B7B5\u2013$B80F, after the input consumed by the scene picture decode."
  }
 ]
